  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AAP2023-Expenditure Verification of one works contract</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The Expenditure Verifier is expected&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;- To carry out the agreed-upon procedures listed in Annex 2 and&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;To issue reports based on the template in Annex 3 which will support the Contracting Authority&apos;s conclusions on the eligibility of the reported expenditure and the related follow-up.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The expenditure verification will be performed as a desk review and fieldwork at the location indicated in Annex 1.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Additional specific objectives in the form of agreed-upon procedures on which the Expenditure Verifier is expected to perform a verification are:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;The expenditure verifier should select a representative sample with value of minimum 65% of all transactions reported with the Final financial report.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;The auditor shall evaluate the technical criteria and specifications for works executed and reported in the verified financial report. For this purpose, the Auditor is requested to use the work of an Auditor&apos;s expert and to obtain sufficient appropriate audit evidence for this work in accordance with ISA 6203. Works executed shall be technically assessed&lt;a href=&quot;#_ftn1&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[1]&lt;/a&gt; and the auditor shall report on compliance of works expenditures reported in the verified report, with:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;-the evaluation of the consistency between the design (measurements, specifications, drawings, bills of quantities) set out in the contract (including any amendment/variation order), the works actually carried out and the actual value of works accounted for in the interim certificates of payment issued by the Supervisor; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;-the evaluation of the quality of the completed works in conformity with the technical specifications set out in the works contract and the invoiced price for the works&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;-the existence and the compliance with the relevant procedures of contractual documents, such as: Administrative Orders, Addendums, Variation Orders, etc.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;-availability of the project(s) management documents such as: work register,&amp;nbsp;including the list of equipment used daily, relevant measurements books, calculation fiches and as-built drawings approved by the supervision team, minutes of site meetings, works planning , the topographical, geotechnical and every other intermediary tasks&apos; acceptance reports, progress reports of the supervising consultant, any other contractual documents and administrative orders, site correspondence and all correspondences between the contractor(s), the supervising consultant(s) and the administration, as required in the contract.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
